From 65d6e751863f670ad7f5890f3faa8b6b33a2a704 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MisterRaindrop <p_xiaoyu.liu@synxdata.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:05:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pax: add a columnar scan interface for datafusion_executor

Expose PAX's micro-partition listing and column decoding through one
exported C function table, datafusion_pax_scan_api(), so that the
datafusion_executor extension can read PAX blocks column by column on its
worker threads instead of row by row through the table AM.  Every other
symbol is local, so nothing can clash with PAX or PostgreSQL.

begin skips micro-partitions and groups by their min/max statistics, as
PAX's own scan does, on the main thread since that calls fmgr.  read_block
hands out fixed-width columns, and strings (text, varchar, bpchar) and
numerics as offsets and bytes, with PAX's toast and the vectorized
format's numerics decoded without PostgreSQL calls.  It reports the
memory it holds (read buffer, decoded columns, visibility map, handed-out
rows) so that the caller can account for it.  block_groups lets callers
spread the groups of one block over several threads.
---
 .../src/cpp/access/datafusion_scan_api.cc     | 512 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../src/cpp/access/datafusion_scan_api.h      | 128 +++++
 2 files changed, 640 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 contrib/pax_storage/src/cpp/access/datafusion_scan_api.cc
 create mode 100644 contrib/pax_storage/src/cpp/access/datafusion_scan_api.h

diff --git a/contrib/pax_storage/src/cpp/access/datafusion_scan_api.cc b/contrib/pax_storage/src/cpp/access/datafusion_scan_api.cc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a923a15
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/pax_storage/src/cpp/access/datafusion_scan_api.cc
