+ *
+ * datafusion_scan_api.cc
+ *	  Read PAX micro-partitions column by column on the caller's threads,
+ *	  bypassing the table AM's row-at-a-time interface.  See
+ *	  datafusion_scan_api.h for the interface and its threading contract.
+ *
+ * datafusion_executor compiles this file into its own library and loads it
+ * after PostgreSQL has loaded pax.so (RTLD_GLOBAL); the PAX classes used
+ * here bind to that pax.so.  They are internal classes, not a published
+ * API, so the library must run with the very pax.so whose headers it was
+ * built with: DF_PAX_BUILD_ID records that pax.so's GNU build ID, and the
+ * caller compares it with the running one.
+ *
+ * Memory: PAX's reader allocates with malloc.  read_block passes PAX a read
+ * buffer of its own (ReaderOptions::reused_buffer, as PAX's scan does) and
+ * reports through 'account' what it can see: that buffer's capacity, the
+ * projected columns' decoded data and null bitmaps, the visibility map and
+ * the rows it hands out.  The file footer and PAX's small bookkeeping
+ * objects are not counted, nor the values PAX decodes for GetDatum (toast,
+ * the vectorized format's strings) until the group is done; uncompressed
+ * columns that point into the read buffer are counted twice.
+ *
+ * contrib/pax_storage/src/cpp/access/datafusion_scan_api.cc
+ *
+ *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ */
